When every component calls APIs directly, your business logic becomes scattered. Let features own communication with the backend — not the UI.

3 min read
5 hours ago

--

Press enter or click to view image in full size

The Easy Way Isn’t Always the Right Way
Angular makes HTTP requests simple.
Inject HttpClient, call an endpoint, and you're done.
export class CustomerPageComponent {private readonly customerApi =
inject(CustomerApiService);
readonly customers = signal<Customer[]>([]);
ngOnInit() {
this.customerApi
.getCustomers()
.subscribe(customers => {
this.customers.set(customers);
});
}
}
It works.
Until another component needs the same data.
Then another.
Then another.
Soon, the same API call is scattered across multiple components.
The Hidden Cost
Imagine these components:
Customer List
Customer Dashboard
Customer Report
Customer Search
Customer ProfileEach one calls:
customerApi.getCustomers()
